| First disk state byte | `0B6Eh..0B6Fh` | 1 | outside character owner |

Service-body inventory: 810 bytes before gateways.
Shared low dispatch/exit code, CMOS helpers, ROM/A20 return gates and
device state are separate. These bodies are not position-independent;
their existing near calls and CS-relative state need explicit bindings.

### Bulk-placement design budget (not achieved savings)

| Candidate | Current bytes | Unproved prerequisite |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| BIOS_SERVICE_START..BIOS_SERVICE_END | 3,578 | split CS-relative low data, near control flow, and ROM-return gates |
| Entire DOS low prefix | 4,480 | subtract mandatory public anchors, stacks, and entry gates |
| Initial DOS-owned HMA tail | 16,892 | subtract COMMAND and every other reservation before choosing destinations |

The candidate sizes are inventories, not guaranteed gains or a sum to
subtract from VC's gap. The HMA tail is capacity, not conventional
memory; copied low allocations must be released and coalesced. Dynamic
SYSINIT allocations require the runtime census, not this linker map.

